course: dictionary
lesson: 2076
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists each meaning separately, so you can check which one fits your sentence. Look at the words around the word to choose the right one. The word constituent is a good example.
explain: In the first meaning, a constituent is one of the parts that make up a whole. «Flour is a constituent of bread.» Flour is one of the parts that bread is made from. In science lessons, the constituents of a mixture are the substances mixed together.
explain: In the second meaning, a constituent is a person who lives in an area and votes for its representative, such as a Member of Parliament or a congressman. «A constituent is a person who lives in the area an MP represents; anyone can write to their MP or member of Congress, including children.» So a constituent is a voter, and even children can write to their MP.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have chosen well. If it does not, try the other meaning.
fact: Constituent can be a noun or an adjective. «Constituent parts» means the parts that make up something.
fact: «Constituent» means one of the parts that make up a whole.
fact: «Constituent» can also mean a person who lives in an area and votes for its MP or congressman.
fact: «The constituents of» a mixture are the substances in it.
fact: Phrases such as «constituent parts» and «the constituents of» help you spot which meaning is being used.
exercise: «Flour is a constituent of bread.» What does constituent mean here? | A type of oven | A tin used for baking | *One of the parts that make up a whole | A person who votes for an MP
exercise: «A constituent is a person who lives in the area an MP represents.» Who is a constituent? | A Member of Parliament who works in London | A member of a school council | *A voter who lives in the area an MP represents | A part of a mixture
exercise: Which phrase is a clue that constituent means a part of something? | *«constituent parts» | «your MP» | «votes on Tuesday» | «write a letter»
test: «The constituents of the paint were mixed carefully.» What does constituents mean here? | *The substances that make up the paint | The tins it came in | The people who painted the wall | The colours on the shelf
test: Maya lives in the area an MP represents and writes to them about a park. What is Maya to that MP? | A part of a mixture | A Member of Parliament | A congressman | *A constituent
exam: In which sentence does constituent mean a voter? | Water is a constituent of ice | *A constituent wrote to her MP about the new bridge | Sugar is a constituent of jam | Oats are a constituent of this cereal
